00:42:34.170 --> 00:42:36.270
- Well, listen, I mean
the equality guarantee

00:42:36.270 --> 00:42:40.180
is that as citizens,
we have the same rights

00:42:40.180 --> 00:42:43.770
to stand before the law and to
participate in our democracy

00:42:43.770 --> 00:42:45.760
as any other citizen does.

00:42:45.760 --> 00:42:49.408
And the country is founded on
this premise and in many ways,

00:42:49.408 --> 00:42:51.940
and this is sort of our
core bedrock guarantee

00:42:51.940 --> 00:42:55.380
that you don't have to be
born to a certain family

00:42:55.380 --> 00:42:56.790
or born in a certain zip code

00:42:56.790 --> 00:42:57.990
or have a certain amount of wealth

00:42:57.990 --> 00:42:59.650
in order to matter in this country.

00:42:59.650 --> 00:43:01.240
And we think that every person matters.

00:43:01.240 --> 00:43:04.040
I look back at, Thomas
Jefferson has this great phrase

00:43:04.040 --> 00:43:07.450
where he says that cultivators
of the earth, farmers,

00:43:07.450 --> 00:43:08.920
are the most valuable to citizens.

00:43:08.920 --> 00:43:10.290
Now I come from a farming family

00:43:10.290 --> 00:43:12.030
so I heard that a lot growing up

00:43:12.030 --> 00:43:14.440
and I tend to agree with it,

00:43:14.440 --> 00:43:17.160
but it was revolutionary
statement at Jefferson's time

00:43:17.160 --> 00:43:19.100
because if you look back in human history,

00:43:19.100 --> 00:43:21.670
people who worked with their
hands were usually dismissed.

00:43:21.670 --> 00:43:23.950
And I was like, "Oh, I
mean, that's manual labor.

00:43:23.950 --> 00:43:26.210
That's for people who can't get educated

00:43:26.210 --> 00:43:27.060
and who aren't smart."

00:43:27.060 --> 00:43:30.482
And the idea that manual
laborers would be a citizen

00:43:30.482 --> 00:43:33.310
and would have a role in
democracy, I mean, absolutely not.

00:43:33.310 --> 00:43:35.140
The Romans for instance, the Greeks,

00:43:35.140 --> 00:43:37.000
they would never allow that.

00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:39.550
Our country is premised on the idea

00:43:39.550 --> 00:43:43.210
that folks who work for
a living are valuable

00:43:43.210 --> 00:43:46.500
and that everybody should stand
as an equal before the law.

00:43:46.500 --> 00:43:48.220
And it's the law that should rule,

00:43:48.220 --> 00:43:49.380
the law made by the people

00:43:49.380 --> 00:43:52.070
and not any particular
person or group of people.

00:43:52.070 --> 00:43:54.810
So that is a long answer, I guess,

00:43:54.810 --> 00:43:57.480
to what I think our core
constitutional commitment is.

00:43:57.480 --> 00:44:01.040
